# Gentoo port: migrations listed here are not applicable on Gentoo. The
# patched bin/omarchy-migrate skips them (logging one line) and marks them
# done, so they neither run nor linger as pending. One filename per line.
#
# 1781984677 — Normalize Snapper snapshot services: repairs the upstream
# limine + snapper snapshot stack, which this overlay intentionally does not
# port (README "intentionally not ported" #2), and which is meaningless on
# non-Btrfs roots.
1781984677.sh
# 1784672586 — pacman transaction swapping quickshell for quickshell-git:
# pointless here (the ::guru quickshell build has the fixed kill behavior
# already) and superseded by 1787399318, which no-ops the same way.
1784672586.sh
# 1785637426 — omarchy-pkg-add omacalc: omacalc is not ported yet (P2
# candidate); the accompanying gnome-calculator drop is not worth a fail.
1785637426.sh
# 1786273938 — omarchy-pkg-add herdr: herdr is not ported (P4, AI ecosystem).
1786273938.sh
# 1786355450 — omarchy-pkg-add ttfx: ttfx is not ported yet (P2 candidate).
1786355450.sh
# 1786952219 — pacman swap of Arch's mise for omarchy's mise-bin: moot here.
# The same payload is dev-util/mise-bin (ported), so package management
# belongs to Portage either way - the swap must not happen.
1786952219.sh
# 1787589206 — edits /etc/pacman.conf, which does not exist on Gentoo; the
# script's final guard then ends the run nonzero and would stay pending
# forever.
1787589206.sh
# 1789325478 — installs the linux-omarchy kernel and a Limine boot entry:
# kernels and the bootloader are the user's on Gentoo (README "intentionally
# not ported" #3).
1789325478.sh
# 1789444024 — installs linux-omarchy/linux-t2 kernel headers: same kernel
# policy as 1789325478.
1789444024.sh
# 1791403252 — edits /etc/pacman.conf to prioritize the Omarchy package
# repository over the Arch repositories: there is no pacman.conf on Gentoo
# (same class as 1787589206), and on Gentoo that priority is inherent - the
# overlay is the package source, Portage owns ordering.
1791403252.sh
# 1788279117 — replaces the YT6801 vendor DKMS driver: upstream exits 1 by
# design when lspci finds no 1f0a:6801 adapter, so it would fail outright on
# every machine without the hardware; the Arch DKMS driver was never
# installable on Gentoo, so there is nothing here to replace either.
1788279117.sh
# 1789764927 — installs owe and owe-lockfeed plus their owed.service hook:
# both are in-house apps with upstream recipes, not ported yet (P3; the
# recipe is a Node/web stack, see helpers/gentoo-skip.tsv for family).
1789764927.sh
# 1790539857 — installs monologue, the webcam recorder: recipe exists
# upstream, port pending (P3 candidate).
1790539857.sh
# 1790542069 — installs hype, the Markdown presentation app: recipe exists
# upstream, port pending (P3 candidate).
1790542069.sh
# 1791542175 — installs gliff, the Hyprland remote desktop over SSH: recipe
# exists upstream, port pending (P3 candidate); the x86 guard passes on this
# overlay's only keyworded arch, so it would run and fail.
1791542175.sh
# 1790702362 — installs the compiler and Qt stack for building Omarchy-style
# apps: Arch's base-devel group has no single Gentoo atom. The rest maps to
# dev-qt/qt{base,declarative,multimedia,svg,wayland}:6 and
# media-video/ffmpeg; emerge them by hand if wanted.
1790702362.sh
# 1791367434 — installs the fcitx5 IME pack: fcitx5-mozc/hangul/chewing are
# Arch package names (Gentoo: app-i18n/mozc with its fcitx5 USE, hangul and
# chewing unmapped), and input-method selection is a per-user choice.
1791367434.sh
# 1791554699 — swaps Arch's power-profiles-daemon for omarchy's CPPC-enabled
# fork via raw pacman: the fork is Arch-only; Gentoo keeps
# sys-power/power-profiles-daemon.
1791554699.sh
# 1791403310 — installs omarchy-hyprland-titlebars: a Hyprland plugin that
# only loads into the exact Hyprland build it was compiled against (upstream
# pins =hyprland-0.57.1 and rebuilds it on every Hyprland change). Gentoo's
# gui-wm/hyprland happens to be 0.57.1 today, but the ebuild would need
# subslot-coupled rebuilds to stay loadable across updates - port pending
# (P3; cosmetic feature).
1791403310.sh
# 1791708587 — installs signed, the PDF signing app: recipe exists upstream,
# port pending (P3 candidate, same class as monologue/hype).
1791708587.sh
# 1791898365 — speeds up the Limine boot menu: this box boots GRUB, so the
# migration is a designed no-op here (no limine.conf to edit). It cannot
# even reach that no-op unattended: its sudo -v probe prompts under the
# passwordless-sudo stack's verifypw=all (the reason omarchy-update's own
# authorize step avoids -v), and an unattended update then dies on the
# password read. Same class would apply to any future sudo -v migration.
1791898365.sh
# Pre-port migrations driving raw pacman (1785013000, 1785351479,
# 1787399318, 1787865477, 1788009111, 1789928586, 1791152480,
# 1791769486): they predate both the Gentoo port and the omarchy-pkg-*
# tools, and every Gentoo install has already settled them - upgraded
# installs ran them during the 4.5.0 migration wave (their pacman paths
# are guarded no-ops there), fresh installs seed all migration markers
# through /etc/skel. Static audit class: raw pacman.
1785013000.sh
1785351479.sh
1787399318.sh
1787865477.sh
1788009111.sh
1789928586.sh
1791152480.sh
1791769486.sh
# 1790973240 — ASUS ProArt P14 speaker firmware: hardware-guarded
# (omarchy-hw-match H7407BA, an aarch64 laptop this ~amd64-only overlay
# can never match) and the vendor firmware package is Arch-only.
1790973240.sh
# 1791077437 — installs linux-omarchy-n1x and its headers: aarch64-guarded
# kernel packages, and kernels are the user's on Gentoo (README
# "intentionally not ported" #3).
1791077437.sh
# 1792041364 — installs gliff on aarch64: hardware-guarded on an arch this
# overlay does not keyword, and the recipe is unported (P3).
1792041364.sh
